nvidia: RTD3 cuts the power as soon as RM has shut the GPU down, with no hold-off (as Linux does)

0002 waited RTD3_HOLDOFF_S (10 s) of idle before the power cut. In COARSE mode RM signals idle only after the last
close has shut the adapter down (nv_stop_device -> nv_shutdown_adapter -> rm_shutdown_adapter, then
rm_unref_dynamic_power -> nv_indicate_idle). So for those 10 s the GPU sat in D0 with RM and the GSP down: powered and
unmanaged. Measured on the ThinkPad X1 Extreme Gen 5 (BE 49, 2026-11-12): +1.0 to +1.6 C/s during each hold-off
(52 -> 68 C in one), while the same GPU held open by RM idles and cools (59 -> 52 C in 20 s). Eight open/close cycles
took it from 51 to 81 C and the thermal guard rebooted the machine.

Linux does not wait: nv_indicate_idle drops the runtime-PM usage count, the GPU endpoint has no autosuspend delay (the
500 ms in nv.c is the Tegra iGPU path only), so it goes to D3hot at once, and the root port's 100 ms autosuspend
(drivers/pci/pcie/portdrv.c) then runs its _PR3 _OFF. The hold-off bought nothing for a reopen: a reopen pays RM init
(3-4 s, GSP boot) in COARSE mode whether or not the rail was cut, and the power-on adds ~0.1 s (link up after 0 ms,
config after +100 ms).

The off task now runs the off as soon as it gets ldata_lock. The last close still holds ldata_lock while RM signals
idle, so the task retries every 10 ms (was 100 ms) and cuts the power ~10 ms after the close returns. The state machine,
the gen/usage_count/INITIALIZED re-checks under ldata_lock and the lock order are unchanged. The off line in the system
log reports the ms since RM signalled idle.

One illumos difference: RM signals the attach-time idle inside attach(9E) (rm_enable_dynamic_power_management), and after
attach returns the parent's DDI_POST ctlop (npe: pf_init, pcie_postattach_child -> pcie_enable_ce) still writes the GPU's
config space. The 10 s hold-off hid that. Linux's PCI core holds a runtime-PM reference across probe; here the task waits
(10 ms retries) until i_ddi_devi_attached(), which the framework sets after the DDI_POST ctlop.

